1. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY & ARCHITECTURE OVERVIEW
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CodeCollab has established a dedicated, centralized, and decoupled `cyber-security/`
folder that orchestrates all defensive controls across the frontend, API gateway,
authentication layer, and data persistence pipelines.

Security concerns are segregated into focused, auditable modules:
- Authentication & Session Security (Ambient HttpOnly cookies + optional Bearer)
- Anti-CSRF Guardrails for state-changing operations
- Origin-normalized CORS policies with preflight caching
- Strict HTTP Security Headers (Content Security Policy, CORP, Frame-Ancestors)
- Declarative Schema Validation with automatic field allowlisting
- Sanitization for user URLs, social links, and profile preferences
- Constant-time cryptographic routines to defeat side-channel timing leaks
- Tiered IP rate limiting for API, authentication, and password endpoints
- Request correlation (UUIDv4) and automated database credential redaction in logs


2. DEDICATED `cyber-security/` DIRECTORY STRUCTURE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
```
cyber-security/
│
├── index.js                  # Central barrel facade exporting all security mechanisms & submodules
├── cookieSecurity.js         # HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite cookie manager (dual localhost & prod HTTPS)
├── csrfProtection.js         # Anti-CSRF verification middleware for state-mutating requests
├── corsConfig.js             # Production CORS configuration, 24h preflight cache & origin normalizer
├── securityHeaders.js        # Strict Helmet CSP, clickjacking defense, CORP, and static shielding
├── authMiddleware.js         # Dual Bearer / HttpOnly session auth + guest optionalAuthMiddleware
├── authorization.js          # Resource ownership, private project boundaries & IDOR defense
├── inputValidation.js        # Strict schema validator, field allowlisting, and validateBody middleware
├── urlSecurity.js            # WHATWG URL sanitizer & XSS protection against dangerous URI schemes
├── preferenceSanitizer.js    # User profile preference merge, sanitizeUserObj & mass-assignment defense
├── cryptoUtils.js            # Bcrypt password hashing, timing-safe equality & constant-time decoy hashing
├── rateLimiter.js            # Tiered rate limiters (API: 500/15m, Auth: 100/15m, Passwords: 15/15m)
├── securityLogger.js         # X-Request-Id correlation, payload error handler, credential scrubbing
├── tests/
│   └── security-suite.test.js # Comprehensive security test suite (100% pass)
└── README.md                 # Complete architectural documentation & threat model
```

Backwards-Compatible Facades:
Existing files under `src/utils/` (`cookieSecurity.js`, `urlSecurity.js`,
`validation.js`, `preferenceMerge.js`) re-export directly from `cyber-security/`,
ensuring zero breakage for legacy services, scripts, and automated test runners.


